# Casual profile: no AMD SEV-SNP encryption or guest attestation on top of base.config's
# universal hardening. (FIPS mode is profile-independent — see hardening.kernel.fips.)

# Compiles Lockdown's active level in, rather than relying on the `lockdown=integrity` cmdline
# flag to set it — LOCKDOWN_LSM_EARLY (self-protection.config) enforces from early boot, but
# only at whatever level this choice resolves to (default: none). A cmdline is the wrong single
# point of failure for that. Can still be raised at runtime via `lockdown=confidentiality`, just
# not lowered below this. Integrity, not confidentiality: casual makes no confidentiality claim
# to begin with (see docs/threat_model.md). sev-snp.config sets confidentiality instead.
CONFIG_LOCK_DOWN_KERNEL_FORCE_INTEGRITY=enable
